    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "BLUF",
      "narration_text": "Lambda feels instant, but your code needs a place to run first. When that place isn't ready, the request waits for setup.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "BrutalistHesitantWriter",
          "props": {
            "text": "Lambda always runs your code instantly.\nSometimes the request waits for setup.",
            "triggerWords": "always runs your code instantly",
            "replacementWords": "sometimes sets up first",
            "face": "serif",
            "fontSize": 62,
            "lineSpacing": 1.25,
            "align": "center",
            "seed": "lambda-cold-start-b01",
            "ink": "#3D3929",
            "accent": "#D97757",
            "bg": "#F2F0E9"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-23T23:30:48.705377+00:00"
          }
        },
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.0,
            "event": "writer types the claim"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.5,
            "event": "corrected to 'sometimes sets up first'"
          }
        ]
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "lead_silence_s": 0.8,
      "actual_duration_s": 7.68
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "COLD",
      "narration_text": "That place is an execution environment: an isolated space with your code, its dependencies and the language runtime. If none is ready, Lambda starts the runtime and runs your initialization code before calling your function. That setup time is a cold start.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "AgentToolLoop",
          "props": {
            "stages": [
              "REQUEST",
              "START RUNTIME",
              "RUN INIT CODE",
              "YOUR FUNCTION"
            ],
            "executeIndex": 1,
            "loopBack": false,
            "ports": [],
            "sparkLine": "Setup before your code."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-23T23:31:56.379014+00:00"
          }
        },
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.05,
            "event": "cold path lights in narration order"
          }
        ]
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.92
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "WARM",
      "narration_text": "After a request, Lambda may keep the environment. The next request can reuse it and skip most setup: that's a warm start. But reuse isn't guaranteed.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "LessonExcerpt",
          "props": {
            "header": "Cold vs warm",
            "subheader": "",
            "rows": [
              {
                "tag": "COLD START",
                "text": "no ready environment, so set one up first",
                "emphasis": true
              },
              {
                "tag": "WARM START",
                "text": "reuse a kept environment and skip most setup"
              },
              {
                "tag": "NO GUARANTEE",
                "text": "environments can be removed"
              }
            ],
            "footer": "Same function, different response times",
            "sparkLine": "Reuse helps, when it happens."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-23T23:33:04.051130+00:00"
          }
        },
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.12,
            "event": "cold"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.32,
            "event": "warm"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.52,
            "event": "no guarantee"
          }
        ]
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.9
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "MATH",
      "narration_text": "When traffic grows, Lambda needs more environments at once: roughly requests per second times seconds per request. A hundred a second at a fifth of a second each needs about twenty, and new ones start cold, even while others are warm.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "TypesetMath",
          "props": {
            "title": "How many environments?",
            "rows": [
              {
                "src": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,",
                "aspect": 5.1714,
                "expression": "N \\approx \\lambda \\times d",
                "at": 1.0
              },
              {
                "src": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,",
                "aspect": 8.0857,
                "expression": "100 \\times 0.2 = 20",
                "at": 6.0
              }
            ],
            "note": "λ: requests per second · d: seconds per request",
            "conditions": "Illustrative numbers — new environments start cold"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-23T23:34:34.791824+00:00"
          }
        },
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.1,
            "event": "N ≈ λ × d"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.45,
            "event": "100 × 0.2 = 20"
          }
        ]
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.04
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FIX",
      "narration_text": "To reduce cold starts, make initialization lighter, or use provisioned concurrency, which prepares environments ahead of time. The trade-off: you pay to keep that capacity ready.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "LessonExcerpt",
          "props": {
            "header": "Fewer cold starts",
            "subheader": "",
            "rows": [
              {
                "tag": "LIGHTER INIT",
                "text": "load less when the environment starts"
              },
              {
                "tag": "PROVISIONED",
                "text": "prepare environments ahead of time",
                "emphasis": true
              },
              {
                "tag": "TRADE-OFF",
                "text": "you pay to keep capacity ready"
              }
            ],
            "footer": "Provisioned concurrency = environments kept initialized",
            "sparkLine": "Ready costs money."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-23T23:35:42.235517+00:00"
          }
        },
        "show": [
